sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant C as Client
    participant H as Handler
    participant S as Store
    participant M as Manager
    participant R as Redis
    participant Recv as Receiver
    C->>H: POST /events/abc + body
    H->>S: Store.Append(events/abc, body)
    S->>R: EVALSHA append.lua · durable append
    R-->>S: OK · new tail
    S-->>H: committed append result
    H->>M: OnStreamAppend(events/abc)
    Note over M: enqueue or coalesce one path<br/>no Redis, tail read, or delivery
    M-->>H: bounded enqueue outcome
    H-->>C: 204 · Stream-Next-Offset
    Note over M,R: The worker may start before or after the response.<br/>The handler does not wait for it.
    M->>R: StreamSubscribers(events/abc) · fanout index
    M->>R: GetMany(subscribers) · pipelined state and links
    M->>R: TailOffsets(distinct links) · batched tails
    Note over M: pure idle-and-pending decision
    M->>R: EVALSHA arm_wake.lua · generation++ · ZADD lease
    Note over M: idle → waking · mint wake_id
    M->>Recv: POST webhook · Webhook-Signature t,kid,ed25519
    Recv-->>M: 200 {done:true}
    M->>R: EVALSHA ack.lua — fence · ack tail · release · manager.go
    Note over R: cursor → tail · waking → idle
